WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.390
<b><i>Keep out!</i></b>

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.070
<i>My name is Komi Shou.</i>

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.720
<b>Komi Shou</b>

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.620
<i>I'm a second year student at Binan High School,</i>

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.490
<i>but for certain reasons, I became a shut-in.</i>

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:18.600
<b>12. Anonymous Shut-in 
I hate it when people talk to 
me when I'm clearly reading</b>

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:18.810
<b>22. Anonymous Shut-in 
It's funny how they 
always come late to meetings</b>

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.720
<b>23. Anonymous Shut-in 
My friend's really picky 
about food, won't eat any meat</b>

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.020
<b>32. Anonymous Shut-in 
>>23 
He probably has another 
reason for that, right?</b>

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:20.760
<b>50. Anonymous Shut-in 
Everyone around me are good people. 
They're all working really hard.</b>

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:20.930
<b>51. Anonymous Shut-in 
Oh, that's cool ^^</b>

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:22.710
<b>65. Anonymous Shut-in 
Friends are a pain in the ass anyway. 
I cut myself off from them (lololololol)</b>

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.330
Are you me?

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:26.270
<b>65. Anonymous Shut-in 
Friends are a pain in the ass anyway. 
I cut myself off from them (lololololol)</b>

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.900
<b>168. Anonymous Shut-in 
>>65 
Good for you, loner</b>

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.060
<b>67. Anonymous Shut-in 
>>65 
Mop up those tears</b>

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.230
<b>69. Anonymous Shut-in 
Don't get desperate on us...</b>

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.360
<b>71. Anonymous Shut-in 
>>65 
You should probably take 
another look at yourself</b>

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:30.360
<b>72. Anonymous Shut-in 
What happened, anyway?</b>

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:30.360
<b>79. Anonymous Shut-in 
Probably nothing.
I bet he's just sulking.</b>

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.720
<b>83. Anonymous Shut-in 
Bet his friends were relieved, too.</b>

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.720
<b>84. Anonymous Shut-in 
True</b>

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:36.870
Damn it! Damn it!

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.610
Who needs friends?! 
I'm better off without them!

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:42.650
I don't need...

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.020
Good evening.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.940
I-I-Intruders!

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.300
We are not intruders.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.200
We are conquerors!

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.070
Now, release the Zundar Needle!

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.660
Donum!

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.510
I... I'll tear it all apart...

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.640
That friendship crap...

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.290
I'll tear it limb from limb!

00:02:53.250 --> 00:02:58.950
Love Wanders

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:05.650
Damn, if I'm late today, 
I'll get called to the faculty office.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.580
So run faster, then!

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.430
<b>Delicious Life Campaign♥</b>

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.430
Hey, sorry. Hang on a minute.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.440
I'm gonna buy some bread.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.930
Oh, what the heck?

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:20.930
<b>Delicious Life Campaign♥</b>

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.440
I'm going on without you!

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.100
<b>Fresh-Baked
Cream Bread</b>

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:43.820
Don't leave me behind!

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.120
You scared me!

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.560
I felt so alone!

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.100
But I was going to be late!

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.140
So you're saying you don't care if I'm late?

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:51.730
But that's why I waited.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.750
You didn't wait! You <i>went</i>!

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.800
I waited by walking slowly!

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.760
What's with you? This is a 
weird thing to pick a fight over.

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.720
You've been really cold lately.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.640
What are you basing that on?

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:07.390
Didn't we have the most fun in history 
together over summer vacation?

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.050
Or maybe we actually got a little too close?

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.370
Why are you talking like such a pain in the ass?

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:13.690
That's right.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.610
I guess I am a pain in the ass.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.870
What's with you, En-chan?

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.560
Did you eat some poisonous
mushrooms or something?

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:22.930
Just...

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.270
Stay away from me.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:25.460
Hey...

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:26.450
Wait!

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:27.680
Don't come this way!

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.010
I have to! I'm going to school, too!

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.900
Kinugawa, you're late.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:38.550
Oh, sorry.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:41.840
Anyway, never forget to check your own work.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.180
But at the same time, be prompt in—

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:46.010
Teacher! My stomach hurts, 
so I'm going to the nurse's office!

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.220
Right after you got here?!

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:50.510
Did I do something wrong?

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:54.530
Not really.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.020
Then is there a reason you said that stuff?

00:04:58.040 --> 00:04:58.940
Not really.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:01.010
Is it because the last time you came over,

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.390
I spent the whole time doing a jigsaw puzzle?

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:04.800
Not really.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.180
"Not really" doesn't tell me anything.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:10.380
Hey, c'mon!

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:12.370
Just leave me alone already!

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:15.840
It's really suffocating when you do that!

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:19.400
Fine.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.680
Box lunch! Box lunch!

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.680
<b>Earth Defense 
Club (lol)</b>

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:39.060
Disappear!

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:42.080
Someone kill me!

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.080
Hey, what are you standing there for?

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:43.150
Whoa, what's he doing?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.470
Is this a new exercise of some kind?

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.030
A fight?!

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:50.850
With Kinugawa-senpai, 
who you're always so close with?

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:51.840
How come?

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.510
I don't know. Maybe it's menopause?

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:56.630
Your face does look old, 
but isn't it a bit early for that?

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:58.720
They say men go through 
menopause too, you know.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.860
You're not even sure if you're 
done with puberty yet.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.190
Oh, I want to disappear!

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:04.030
See, that kind of thing is definitely puberty.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:07.930
Why not just say you're sorry and make up?

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:10.740
It's nice that you can 
take everything so lightly.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:14.510
I agree that a prompt 
apology is the best strategy!

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:17.540
Spaces without love render the heart empty!

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:19.690
Even Wombat is lecturing me...

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:24.470
That pitch... He's coming!

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:29.750
Yo.

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:30.610
Hello there.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:31.130
Hey.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:32.870
Lunch?

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.580
I'm about to get started, too!

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.050
Yeah, on your second.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:42.690
No, I'll eat in the cafeteria today.

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.420
I just came to pick up something I forgot.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:45.590
Later.

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:50.190
Hey, is it true you had a 
fight with En-chan-senpai?

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.350
<i>Right to the point?!</i>

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:55.760
I don't know about a fight. 
I think he's just sulking.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:02.780
Then you should go offer to 
make up with him, Atsushi-senpai!

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.110
I'd better pass for now.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:09.620
Sometimes it's best to let sleeping dogs lie.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:15.040
Are you really okay with that?!

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:15.910
En-cha—

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:18.370
You should care more about me! 
Be more persistent!

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:19.990
That's totally different 
from what you said before!

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:22.210
You're really cold for someone 
whose name means "warm," you know.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.470
Don't bring my name into this! 
I'm really worried about you!

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:25.820
Hey, hey...

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:26.900
Am I suffocating you, or do you 
want me to care more? Which is it?

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:30.480
Both! Humans are contradictory, after all!

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:31.460
That's a pain in the ass!

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:32.400
Yeah, that's right!

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:34.020
Hey, c'mon, cut it out!

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:37.520
Don't worry, Yumoto. 
It's between me and En-chan.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:39.760
That's just it.

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:42.440
Why can't you be that 
thoughtful with me, I wonder?

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:45.440
I'm trying to be nice to you, too.

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:46.850
Is that so?

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:50.410
I know the excitement you show in 
the emails you send to me and Yumoto

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:53.620
are on totally different levels!

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:58.960
Your replies to me are always
less than five words long!

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.360
Unlike yours, Yumoto's emails

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.030
aren't just bare-bones random 
sentences with no punctuation!

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:05.700
Plus, they come attached 
with excited emoticons!

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:08.310
Don't you think I should 
respond to that in kind?

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:11.500
By the way, have you been 
stealing my phone to look at it?!

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:11.500
The presence or absence of 
emoticons shows your favoritism!

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:13.790
Send me emails with emoticons sometimes!

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:15.760
Then send me emails of 
a decent length sometimes!

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:18.100
So have you been looking 
at my phone or not? Well?

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:19.040
I guess this <i>is</i> a fight, but...

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.450
What if I have?!

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:23.040
It's the type it doesn't 
pay to interfere with, right?

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:20.540
I'd say you're a jerk!

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.780
Then say it! Show your 
contempt for how pathetic I am!

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:24.320
So you admit it, you jerk!

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.280
U-Um, you guys...

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:29.780
Why not leave it at that and have lunch?

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:30.930
No, thanks.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.450
<b>Binan High School</b>

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.680
I've got to get them to make up somehow.

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.690
Three girls a day... No, day and night...

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.480
To cut my losses or not?

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.080
I have it! Here!

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.090
Stop making noise.

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.360
You're not cut out for that.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:12.110
Come on, everyone, think seriously!

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.640
There are things you think seriously about?

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:18.040
Those two will probably be fine, 
even if we don't worry about it.

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.180
They won't be fine at all!

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:22.100
They said they didn't even want lunch!

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.280
You can't say you don't want food!

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:25.630
It's a serious affair!

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:27.500
Yeah, Yumoto never changes.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:31.050
I keep thinking, but it 
just makes my head hurt!

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.400
I'm gonna go!

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.190
Where?

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:34.010
To see them!

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:41.600
Such determination... 
Maybe we should learn from him.

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:47.070
<b>Kusatsu Kinshiro
Born September 12th
Blood Type A / Virgo
Hobbies: Archery
Likes: Sanjusangendo Temple, 
Kintsuba, Amanatto</b>

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:48.930
What?

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:50.900
Kinugawa and that guy?

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.560
It seems so.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:56.180
Currently, Kinugawa is walking 
to and from school by himself.

00:09:56.180 --> 00:10:00.150
Yufuin comes to school, 
but he barely attends class,

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:03.140
and I'm told that even when they 
cross paths, they don't speak.

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:05.270
I see.

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:11.710
Th-That's good, is it?

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:13.530
However,

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:17.120
the first year boy, Hakone Yumoto-kun,

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:20.130
is attempting to get them to reconcile.

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:22.500
I really dislike that little fluff-head.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.150
He appears to lack any delicacy.

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:30.520
It seems the effects of the monster we 
controlled are finally showing themselves.

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:36.320
This time, by placing the monster in an 
establishment that humans use frequently,

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:40.000
we can distribute the negative 
energy with greater efficiency.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:44.050
And the stronger the friendship, 
the greater the effect.

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:45.960
Fight-causing radio waves.

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:51.380
If we continue to destroy the bonds 
between those who are close...

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:55.860
Then we shall acquire the
wonderful world we've always wanted!

00:10:55.860 --> 00:10:57.880
It's catching. The speech pattern is catching.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.650
<b>Earth Defense Club                        (lol)</b>

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:03.600
How am I going to get them to make up?

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:07.570
If you're too persistent, won't it 
just make the problem worse?

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:11.280
Just telling them to make up 
over and over lacks subtlety.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.670
It's not just that!

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:16.240
I also asked what we're going to do 
about the Battle Lovers and stuff.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:18.160
Wh-What?

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.620
I quit. It's a pain in the ass.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:22.120
Actually, it's always been a pain in the ass.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.980
I'll help out if you really need me,

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:27.240
but I might not feel like 
transforming for a while.

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:29.440
...they said.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:31.570
I've had enough!

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:34.060
Is it always going to be one step forward 
and one step back with you people?!

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:37.260
It's because you forced us to transform
without giving us time to object.

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:40.220
But to begin with, 
I've been smelling it for a while.

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:43.730
The scent of some kind of 
advanced scientific technology plot!

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:45.740
You're saying a monster is behind this?

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:46.720
Bingo!

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:50.100
But we haven't received one 
of those unpleasant alarms.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:54.240
It could be too weak to detect, 
or it could be a momentary power.

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:56.190
A stealth monster, huh?

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:57.680
Okay!

00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:01.080
In that case, I'll go over the 
school with a fine-toothed comb!

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:04.640
Why are you so determined 
to do that kind of legwork?

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:06.670
Running around randomly won't do any good.

00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:09.080
But if we beat the monster, they'll make up!

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.850
I can't just stand around!

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:15.010
If we consider people who might have
been affected by this, I do have a lead.

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:16.920
Kikuchi and Akutagawa from class A, right?

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.360
So you noticed?

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:20.420
They've been arguing since that day, too, right?

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:21.890
Where are you going?

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:24.360
To search for a monster.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:25.850
Using our heads.

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:31.820
He's the one who decided to go shopping,

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:33.870
but once he got back 
from the convenience store,

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.280
he got all angry, like, "what am I, your gofer?"

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:39.180
I was reading Chanporon
at the convenience store,

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:41.150
when he looked over at me and laughed.

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:43.920
And it occurred to me maybe
he was actually a Makachin fan,

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:45.280
and suddenly I couldn't stand it...

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:47.700
Our friend went to the convenience store and...

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:49.670
I was at the convenience store when...

00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:51.620
It was at the convenience store.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.600
The enemy's a convenience store?

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.190
It... seems so.

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:56.630
I'm gonna go check!

00:12:57.860 --> 00:12:59.730
Atsushi-senpai! Atsushi-senpai!

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:01.830
Atsushi-sen-pai-sen!

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:02.980
Paisen?

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:06.580
Did you go to the convenience store near 
the school before your fight started?

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:08.900
How did you know that?

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.310
You did?!

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:12.480
En-chan went in to buy some bread.

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.530
That must be it!

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:16.370
The culprit is in the convenience store!

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:18.880
Spontaneous Love Making!

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:43.610
The Sparkling Prince!

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:45.760
Battle Lover Scarlet!

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:48.790
We are the heirs to the throne of love!

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:51.730
Oh, wait, it's just me!

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:53.690
Atsushi-senpai, I...

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:57.280
I swear I'll get you two to make up!

00:14:01.310 --> 00:14:04.660
It was a monster, then?

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:09.110
Pardon me!

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:10.770
Welcome—

00:14:10.770 --> 00:14:11.700
Cosplay?

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.290
Is there a monster here?

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:14.540
A... monster?

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:17.420
No, I'm afraid we don't carry those here.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:20.590
That's weird. This has to be the place.

00:14:24.780 --> 00:14:26.670
Oh, that's my son.

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:28.550
He's taking time off from school...

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.470
I've got it!

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:32.990
Above the convenience store!

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:37.700
This is it! Pardon me!

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:42.740
What a big kotatsu...

00:14:46.140 --> 00:14:47.700
Who are you?

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:51.160
Come out of there! I'm gonna love you!

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:52.290
No!

00:14:53.020 --> 00:14:55.600
It's not good for you to stay locked up all day!

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:56.620
No!

00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:59.080
Damn. In this case...

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:06.240
Love Stick!

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:10.050
Scarlet Lumiere!

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.860
Huh? Where's Yumoto?

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:14.990
Is there a monster?

00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:15.650
No...

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:24.140
Did I go a little overboard?

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:33.890
What's that?

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:38.460
They're...

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:44.710
Ow, ow...

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:47.580
Th-The school...

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:50.230
What?

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:52.080
School...

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:54.180
No!

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:57.900
I hate school!

00:15:57.900 --> 00:15:58.960
Look out!

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:05.630
This guy's stronger than he looks!

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:07.390
And he keeps getting bigger!

00:16:07.390 --> 00:16:09.780
He's the type that gets harder to 
control as he gets angry, I guess.

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:13.820
Give back En-chan!

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.950
Epinard Hurricane!

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:22.870
What?

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:26.250
Give back my can't-be-bothered, listless En-chan!

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:38.840
Epinard!

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:51.550
What?

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:53.200
Cerulean-senpai!

00:16:54.460 --> 00:16:55.710
Cerulean...

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:57.840
You need to eat more! You're too light!

00:16:57.840 --> 00:16:58.830
Huh?!

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:02.340
Yay! He's back to normal 
even though we haven't beaten it!

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:03.650
I'm not back!

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:05.590
I'm not back...

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:09.210
Even now, I'm really pissed off.

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:11.120
Then why...?

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:14.140
I might be pissed off... 
But even more than that...

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:21.770
I'm furious at myself for nearly losing 
my best friend to such a stupid fight!

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:32.830
D-Don't say "best friend"...

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:33.950
It's embarrassing!

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:39.780
Cerulean!

00:17:40.050 --> 00:17:41.660
Nyah nyah!

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.270
What's embarrassing?

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:49.040
Yourself, because you can't 
call a best friend a best friend?

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:51.780
You piss me off!

00:17:56.020 --> 00:17:57.240
You idiot!

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:01.510
Hey!

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:03.570
I get it.

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:06.490
This does make me want to pick a fight.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:08.770
Atsushi...

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:10.320
But...

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:13.490
Not right now!

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:18.120
That's right!

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:43.970
Epinard Hurricane!

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:46.430
Cerulean Aqua!

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:52.860
Why? Why didn't my radio waves work on you?

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.320
Hey! Use the Love Attack!

00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:58.880
Huh? Oh, roger that!

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:01.760
Sparkle, Lumiere of Love!

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:04.240
Flash, Purifying Aqua!

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:06.740
Pierce, Gallant Hurricane!

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:09.250
Roar, Raging Gaia!

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:11.760
Thrill, Blazing Ignit!

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:16.710
This time, you two can 
deal out the finishing move!

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:18.470
Okay, let's do it!

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:28.330
Love Attack!

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:40.400
So... So cold...

00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:42.020
My blanket...

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:46.860
The cold you feel is something 
no blanket can stave off.

00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:49.460
You understand that too, don't you?

00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:54.890
Love Shower!

00:20:00.990 --> 00:20:04.010
What is this sensation?

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:06.130
Comfort... Healing...

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:09.150
I see... so this is... love.

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:15.110
Love is over.

00:20:15.550 --> 00:20:16.360
Huh?

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:19.320
Isn't that the transfer student, Komi?

00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:20.780
You know him?

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:21.640
Yeah.

00:20:21.640 --> 00:20:24.160
He transferred here at the end of the first term.

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:26.700
At the beginning of the second term, 
he was out of school with the flu...

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:29.030
And he just stopped coming after that.

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:31.070
His house is above a 
convenience store, right?

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:32.450
Hey.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:37.650
I'm really sorry!

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.380
I'm really, really sorry!

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:41.830
I know I wasn't myself, 
but I was totally messed up!

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:43.940
No, no, I'm the one who should apologize.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:45.920
I didn't even notice a monster was behind it.

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:47.840
No, no, it's still my fault.

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:49.220
No, no, I'm at fault, too.

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:51.550
No, no, no, I'm triple at fault.

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:53.500
No, no, I'm at fault cubed.

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:54.800
I feel like everything I did was wasted effort.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.800
No, no, no, no...

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:57.200
Oh well! It worked out okay!

00:20:57.200 --> 00:20:58.580
Not a care in the world, huh?

00:20:58.580 --> 00:21:00.500
Maybe we should learn from him.

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:01.710
Hey, don't cling to me.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:03.990
You're heavy!

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:08.780
<b>Kurotama Bath</b>

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:13.580
That's right, I've been 
completely forgetting my cuddles!

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:14.780
I'm sorry!

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:17.740
I wish you'd forgotten them forever!

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:21.760
Komi said his house was so old, 
it was due for a remodeling anyway.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:25.150
That's very convenient... 
I mean, quite a silver lining.

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:28.180
Once his house is cleaned up, 
he says he'll have some friends over.

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:29.590
That's nice.

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:31.600
Even so...

00:21:32.380 --> 00:21:35.020
No, no. It's my fault 
for erasing your save data.

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:38.730
No, no. It's my fault for getting 
to level 100 on a game you owned.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:41.930
No, no. It's my fault for getting 
potato chips all over your bed.

00:21:41.930 --> 00:21:44.570
No, no. It's my fault for secretly
swapping my seat with yours in class

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:45.690
just because mine was wobbly.

00:21:45.690 --> 00:21:46.490
What, seriously?

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:48.910
No, no. It's my fault for secretly 
looking at your cell phone.

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:49.950
How long will they keep that up 
before they're satisfied?

00:21:48.910 --> 00:21:49.950
Actually, yeah.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:51.360
Fine, I won't do it anymore.

00:21:51.360 --> 00:21:53.660
I'm done for!

00:21:56.880 --> 00:21:58.450
En-chan, you're incredible.

00:21:58.450 --> 00:21:59.350
How so?

00:21:59.350 --> 00:22:02.460
You did something I could never do, 
and totally offhanded. It's amazing.

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:05.060
What's with you? What is it you want?

00:22:05.060 --> 00:22:06.020
Fruit milk?

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:09.390
No, I already got some.

00:23:41.010 --> 00:23:43.890
You know, people don't look at 
you as much as you think they do.

00:23:44.170 --> 00:23:46.660
Not that it matters to me at all.

00:23:46.660 --> 00:23:48.080
Hey, let's eat some melon.

00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:55.010
Next Time

00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:55.010
Love is Stronger than Pride

00:23:48.700 --> 00:23:51.090
Next time: Love is Stronger than Pride.

00:23:51.090 --> 00:23:52.340
Conquest!
